# Relaunch after changes

After making any code changes in this project, relaunch the app so the user can test immediately.

## Command

Run in the background after finishing implementation:

```bash
cd ~/Projects/chinese-tracker && pkill -f "flutter_tools.*run" 2>/dev/null || true; sleep 1; flutter run -d chrome
```

Demo teacher/student content is per-teacher (`AppConstants.contentOwnerFor`) and
does **not** require `--dart-define=CONTENT_OWNER_ID`. Only set that define if
an admin needs an explicit content-owner override when *creating* library items.

## When to relaunch

- After UI, feature, or bug-fix changes
- After router, model, or Firestore service updates
- Skip only for docs-only or comment-only edits with no runtime effect

## Notes

- Do not ask the user to relaunch manually unless the command fails
- Briefly confirm when the app is running again
